From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: validate the complete SOE IPv4 header

IPv4 options extend the header beyond the base 20 bytes. Validate IHL
and pull the full header before returning the skb to IP output, whose
checksum helper reads iph->ihl words. Use that same length for the
transport offset. Reject undersized IHL and truncated options without
changing valid IPv4 or fixed IPv6 header handling.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -790,7 +790,11 @@
 
 	switch (skb->data[0] & 0xf0) {
 	case 0x40:
-		hdr_len = sizeof(struct iphdr);
+		if (!pskb_may_pull(skb, sizeof(struct iphdr)))
+			return -EINVAL;
+		hdr_len = (skb->data[0] & 0x0f) * 4;
+		if (hdr_len < sizeof(struct iphdr))
+			return -EINVAL;
 		skb->protocol = htons(ETH_P_IP);
 		break;
 	case 0x60:
